          {
            "dataId": 3862561,
            "name": "TextArea89",
            "text": "<strong>Study Procedures & Methods</strong>",
            "description": "<ol><li>Explain the study design and choice of methodology (may include a study schema to illustrate)</li><li>Describe any measures taken to eliminate bias</li><li>State the study duration/timeline</li><li>If there is incomplete disclosure, deception, placebo, or a sham procedure, provide the rationale, the process, and any de-briefing measures.</li><li>All tools and study measures must be identified and described. For surveys, focus groups, or interviews ? clarify whether question items and measures are standardized, published, or designed specifically for this research. (This should NOT be any sensitive or triggering line of questioning or discussion)</li><li>Describe the study activities, including The procedures and/or tasks to be performed, Administration of questionnaires, surveys, etc., The data that will be collected</li><li>&nbsp;Indicate what study activities happen when, including, when applicable, a study schedule that notes the number and length of study visits for subjects.</li><li>If there is more than one study session or visit, you may include a schedule of assessments chart to illustrate which procedures occur at a visit. (See Guidance document on our website)* add hyperlink</li><li>Be specific in providing what data points will be collected and describe how data will be transferred/obtained to allow for evaluation of data confidentiality.&nbsp;</li></ol>",
            "required": false,
            "helpText": "",
            "label": "",
            "type": "textarea",
            "dependencies": [
              {
                "targetId": 3862484,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862502,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
