          {
            "dataId": 3862575,
            "name": "TextArea27",
            "text": "<strong>Inclusion/Exclusion criteria & chart identification process</strong>",
            "description": "<ol><li>Inclusion criteria: define the characteristics of patients whose charts will be reviewed in your study. They ensure your study population is relevant to your research question.&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>See the help text (?) for more details.</strong></em></li><li>Exclusion criteria define characteristics that disqualify a patient's chart from your review, even if they meet some inclusion criteria.&nbsp;<em><strong>See the help text (?) for more details.</strong></em></li><li>Explain the process for identifying medical records for the study and who will carry out the process.&nbsp;</li><li>Where are the existing records being obtained from (e.g., medical records, research databases, public records)?</li><li>Did the original data collection involve informed consent for secondary research use?</li><li> If identifiable information is present, what specific de-identification procedures will be used to protect participant privacy?</li></ol>",
            "required": false,
            "helpText": "Here's what to consider when developing inclusion criteria:<br><ul><li><strong>Demographics:</strong> Age range, gender, ethnicity, etc.</li><li><strong>Diagnosis:</strong> Specific diagnoses or related conditions relevant to your study.</li><li><strong>Procedures:</strong> Specific procedures or interventions received.</li><li><strong>Dates:</strong> Date of diagnosis, treatment, or admission window for chart review.</li><li><strong>Medical History:</strong> Specific co-morbidities or past medical history relevant to your study.</li></ul>Reasons for exclusion could be:<br><ul><li><strong>Incomplete records:</strong> Charts missing crucial information for your study.</li><li><strong>Wrong diagnosis:</strong> Patients with diagnoses not relevant to your study question.</li><li><strong>Alternative procedures:</strong> Patients receiving different approaches compared to your study focus.</li><li><strong>Timeframe:</strong> Charts outside the designated date range.</li><li><strong>Consent issues:</strong> Lack of proper informed consent for research use of data.</li></ul><strong>Remember:</strong><br><ul><li>Be specific and clear in defining both inclusion and exclusion criteria.</li><li>Pilot test your criteria on a small sample to refine them if needed.</li><li>Ensure your criteria are relevant to your research question and generate a focused study population.</li></ul>",
            "label": "",
            "type": "textarea",
            "dependencies": [
              {
                "targetId": 3862532,
                "type": "displayed"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862576,
            "name": "TextBox36",
            "text": "<strong>Total Number of Charts</strong><br>",
            "description": "Please list the total number of charts the study plans to review/enroll.<br><br><em>If the study needs to increase this number after the study team receives an exempt determination, a modification can be submitted to increase the number of charts.&nbsp;</em>",
            "required": false,
            "helpText": "",
            "label": "",
            "type": "textbox",
            "dependencies": [
              {
                "targetId": 3862532,
                "type": "displayed"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862577,
            "name": "TextArea28",
            "text": "<strong>Study Design & Methodology</strong>",
            "description": "<ol><li>Specify if the study is a retrospective, prospective (or both) chart review the study team will conduct (e.g., case series, case-control study, cohort study). Explain the rationale for choosing the desired design.</li><li>Describe the procedure for obtaining data. Specify the source of the medical records(e.g., specific hospital, electronic health record system).</li><li>Elaborate on the meticulous data collection process, including the timeframe for chart selection(e.g., past five years); Data abstraction procedures (how data will be extracted from the charts), to instill a sense of thoroughness in the research.</li><li>List all specific variables (data points) the study plans to collect from charts. Define each variable operationally (how it will be measured or categorized). Indicate if the data is already coded in the charts or needs manual abstraction.</li><li>Describe the plan for data storage and security (e.g., de-identification procedures, password protection).</li><li>Specify the software or statistical methods you will use for data analysis.</li><li>Explain how the study will ensure patient confidentiality and privacy throughout the study (Compliance with HIPAA).</li><em><strong>Every question must be addressed, or the application will be returned for changes.&nbsp;</strong></em></ol>",
            "required": false,
            "helpText": "",
            "label": "",
            "type": "textarea",
            "dependencies": [
              {
                "targetId": 3862532,
                "type": "displayed"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "dataId": 3862578,
                "name": "AttachButton18",
                "text": "Attach a data collection form (MS EXCEL) and list all elements or identifiers to be collected as a part of the study.",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "attachment"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862579,
            "name": "TextArea91",
            "text": "<strong>Cost & Compensation</strong>",
            "description": "Please explain:&nbsp;<br><ol><li>If participants will incur any cost to them or their insurance to participate in the study.</li><li>Will participants be compensated for their time and effort participating in this study? (gift cards, course credit, extra credit, SONA credit, etc.) Please explain.&nbsp;</li></ol>",
            "required": false,
            "helpText": "",
            "label": "",
            "type": "textarea",
            "dependencies": [
              {
                "targetId": 3862484,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862502,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862511,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862509,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862514,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
