                      }
                    ],
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "dataId": 3862635,
                        "name": "Radio110",
                        "text": "Yes",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "radio"
                      },
                      {
                        "dataId": 3862636,
                        "name": "Radio111",
                        "text": "No",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "radio"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862637,
                    "name": "Group81",
                    "text": "Will LARs be included in the study population?",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "compoundType": "radio",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "question",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862633,
                        "type": "required"
                      },
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862633,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ],
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "dataId": 3862638,
                        "name": "Radio112",
                        "text": "Yes",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "radio"
                      },
                      {
                        "dataId": 3862639,
                        "name": "Radio113",
                        "text": "No",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "radio"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862640,
                "name": "CheckBox51",
                "text": "Other",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862641,
                    "name": "TextBox18",
                    "text": "Please describe.",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "textbox",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862640,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862642,
            "name": "TextBox19",
            "text": "<strong>Number of Participants</strong>",
            "description": "First, please list the <strong>total</strong> number of participants expected to enroll in the study (this should be an approximate number only).<br><strong><br>Note: &nbsp;</strong><em>You may also include a breakdown if you have multiple populations you plan to enroll. (How many children, parents, various student populations, etc.)&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><br>Example: 50; 25 children, 25 parents</em>",
            "required": true,
            "helpText": "",
            "label": "",
            "type": "textbox"
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862643,
            "name": "TextBox20",
            "text": "If this is a multi-site study with a Reliance Agreement pending IRB approval and TCU IRB will serve as the IRB of Record, list the total number of participants through all study sites.",
            "required": false,
            "helpText": "",
            "label": "",
            "type": "textbox",
            "dependencies": [
              {
                "targetId": 3862404,
                "type": "displayed"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862644,
            "name": "TextArea6",
            "text": "<strong>Inclusion Criteria</strong>",
            "description": "Please<strong>&nbsp;describe and justify</strong>&nbsp;the inclusion criteria.&nbsp;<br>Clearly state the characteristics or attributes that potential participants<strong> must</strong> possess to be eligible for the study.<br> For Example:<br><ul><li>age, gender, ethnicity</li><li> medical conditions (specific diagnosis, disease stage) or&nbsp;</li><li>other relevant characteristics that make enrolling a person/population to participate in this study appropriate&nbsp;</li></ul>It's crucial to use objective and measurable criteria whenever possible. This will ensure the credibility and reliability of the study. Please explain how the chosen criteria directly relates to the research question and objectives.<br><br>",
            "required": true,
            "helpText": "",
            "label": "",
            "type": "textarea"
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862645,
            "name": "TextArea7",
            "text": "<strong>Exclusion Criteria</strong>",
            "description": "&nbsp;Please<strong> describe and justify </strong>the exclusion criteria.&nbsp;<em>Each <strong>e</strong><strong>xclusion criterion must be well-defined and well-justified</strong> by the Investigator. See help text <strong>(?)</strong> for more information.</em><br>&nbsp;Clearly state the characteristics or attributes that will <strong>disqualify</strong> potential participants from the study.<br>For Example:<br><ul><li>History of severe or unstable medical conditions (e.g., heart failure, liver disease, kidney disease)</li><li>Significant cognitive impairment that would prevent participation in study assessments</li><li>Pregnant or breastfeeding women</li></ul>It's crucial to use objective and measurable criteria whenever possible.&nbsp;Explain the rationale behind each exclusion criterion. Common reasons include:<ul><li>Safety concerns (e.g., excluding individuals with certain medical conditions that could increase the risk of adverse events)</li><li>Potential confounding factors (e.g., excluding individuals with comorbidities that could interfere with the interpretation of study results)</li><li>Practical considerations (e.g., excluding individuals who are unlikely to adhere to study procedures or complete follow-up)</li></ul>",
            "required": true,
            "helpText": "<strong>Note* It is important to understand that exclusion criterion are not the opposite of inclusion criteria. For example: If inclusion criteria are female, over age 18, and having a diagnosis of hypertension, exclusion criteria are not male, under 18, and not having a diagnosis of hypertension. Persons excluded from a study like this might be females who meet inclusion criteria but who are pregnant, nursing, or have a co-morbid diagnosis of diabetes.<br><br></strong><strong>Additional Considerations:</strong><br><ul><li><strong>Balance:</strong> Strive for a balance between being inclusive enough to recruit an adequate sample size and being selective enough to ensure a homogenous study population that minimizes confounding factors.</li><li><strong>Ethical Considerations:</strong> Ensure that exclusion criteria are not discriminatory or unfairly exclude certain groups without a valid scientific or ethical reason.</li></ul>",
            "label": "",
            "type": "textarea"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "dataId": 3862646,
        "name": "Section8",
        "text": "Recruitment & Screening",
        "label": "",
        "type": "question",
        "dependencies": [
          {
            "targetId": 3862423,
            "type": "displayed"
          }
        ],
        "children": [
          {
            "dataId": 3862647,
            "name": "Group73",
            "text": "<strong>Recruitment Methods</strong>",
            "description": "<em>Please check off all recruitment methods that will be used as a part of the study.&nbsp; Please ensure all methods used as part of the recruitment process are described.</em>",
            "required": false,
            "helpText": "",
            "compoundType": "checkbox",
            "label": "",
            "type": "question",
            "children": [
              {
                "dataId": 3862648,
                "name": "CheckBox141",
                "text": "Flyers or Advertisments",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox"
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862649,
                "name": "CheckBox142",
                "text": "Emails or Letters",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox"
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862650,
                "name": "CheckBox143",
                "text": "Social Media Platforms&nbsp;<em>See</em>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://research.tcu.edu/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Using-Social-Media-for-Recruitment-Guidance_3.2024.docx\" target=\"_blank\">Social Media for Recruitment&nbsp;Guidance</a>",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox"
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862651,
                "name": "CheckBox144",
                "text": "Crowdsourced research platforms (e.g. MTurk or Prolific)",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox"
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862652,
                "name": "CheckBox145",
                "text": "Scripted presentations/ Verbal Scripts",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox"
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862653,
                "name": "CheckBox171",
                "text": "Word of mouth/ snowball sampling",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox"
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862654,
                "name": "CheckBox146",
                "text": "SONA (&nbsp;<a href=\"https://cse.tcu.edu/psychology/undergraduate/sona-systems.php\" target=\"_blank\">TCU Psychology Department Research Pool</a> (SONA system) or <a href=\"https://tcu-neeley.sona-systems.com/Default.aspx?ReturnUrl=%2f\" target=\"_blank\">Neely School of Business Research Pool</a>",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox"
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862655,
                "name": "CheckBox148",
                "text": "Exisiting Records:&nbsp;Recruitment list, databases, and repositories",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox"
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862656,
                "name": "CheckBox149",
                "text": "Third-party (Non-study Team member) assistance Or a<br>contact from an organization be distributing recruitment materials to potential participants on your behalf, on or off-campus",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox"
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862657,
                "name": "CheckBox219",
                "text": "Screening for eligibility",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox"
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862658,
                "name": "CheckBox217",
                "text": "Collect Personally Identifiable Information for recruitment purposes",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox"
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862659,
                "name": "CheckBox218",
                "text": "Collect Protected Health Information for recruitment purposes",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862660,
                    "name": "Label23",
                    "text": "<em>If study recruitment procedures involve access to PHI (Protected Health Information), HIPAA authorization must be obtained, or a partial waiver of individual HIPAA authorization for recruitment purposes must be granted. By selecting this option you are indicating that information regarding how HIPAA authorization will be addressed is being provided in the HIPAA (Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act) section.</em><br><br><em><strong>NOTE:</strong><br><ul><li><em>Texas Christian University considers the accessing of PHI for purposes preparatory to research to constitute a human subject research activity subject to review and approval or exemption by an authorized IRB.</em></li><li><em>It is not permissible to begin the research by gathering preliminary data via lookups in clinical information systems or reviewing clinical appointment logs or other records of clinical care, prior to IRB review and approval of a study.</em></li></ul></em>",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "label",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862659,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862661,
                "name": "CheckBox150",
                "text": "Other",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862662,
                    "name": "TextBox17",
                    "text": "<em>Please describe.</em>",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "textbox",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862661,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862663,
            "name": "TextArea1",
            "text": "<strong>Recruitment Process<br></strong>",
            "description": "Please provide:<br><ul><li>&nbsp;A <strong>complete and detailed</strong> description&nbsp;of all recruitment procedures and processes. This must be&nbsp;a thorough and comprehensive explanation of the recruitment procedures, instilling confidence in the study's methodology.</li><li>Include methods of when, where, and how potential subjects will be identified&nbsp;and recruited, where the potential participants will be approached, and by whom.&nbsp;</li><li>Describe how all&nbsp;recruitment materials will used to recruit participants.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul><em>Additional Considerations:<br><br></em><ol><li><em>How will the study be introduced to potential participants? And by who?&nbsp;</em></li><li><em>Explain what recruitment materials or methods will be utilized in the recruitment effort.</em></li><li><em>Where will recruitment take place?&nbsp;</em></li><li><em>How will potential participants indicate their interest in the study? (initiate contact with PI or study team)</em></li><li><em>What information, if any, will the study need to collect as a part of the recruitment effort?</em></li><li><em>How will participant privacy and confidentiality be protected during recruitment?<br></em></li><li><em>If applicable, please describe any special considerations or safeguards in place for recruiting vulnerable populations.<br></em></li><li><em>Please address any anticipated challenges or barriers to recruitment and how they will be overcome.<br></em></li><li><em>Cover all relevant aspects of the recruitment process, from initial identification to final enrollment.</em></li></ol>",
            "required": true,
            "helpText": "",
            "label": "",
            "type": "textarea",
            "dependencies": [
              {
                "targetId": 3862648,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862654,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862649,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862650,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862651,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862652,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862658,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862659,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862656,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862653,
                "type": "displayed"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862664,
            "name": "TextArea75",
            "text": "<strong>Existing Records</strong>",
            "description": "Please address each of the following questions applicable to the research.<br><br><ol><li>Where are the existing records being obtained from&nbsp;(e.g., medical records, research databases, public records)?</li><li>Explain the process for identifying medical records for the study and who will carry out the process.&nbsp;</li><li>Did the original data collection involve informed consent for secondary research use?</li><li>&nbsp;If identifiable information is present, what specific de-identification procedures will be used to protect participant privacy?&nbsp;</li><li>If the existing records were collected through a previous research study, was that study approved by an IRB?   If so, did the original IRB approval address using the data for secondary research?</li></ol>",
            "required": false,
            "helpText": "",
            "label": "",
            "type": "textarea",
            "dependencies": [
              {
                "targetId": 3862655,
                "type": "displayed"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862665,
            "name": "AttachButton8",
            "text": "Please attach all recruitment material(s) (e.g., emails, flyers, advertisements, verbal scripts, etc.).&nbsp;<em>Please reference the </em><a href=\"https://research.tcu.edu/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Recruitment-Guidelines_celan-20243.docx\" target=\"_blank\">TCU IRB Recruitment Guidelines</a><em> for the required elements. TCU </em><a href=\"https://research.tcu.edu/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/TCU-Email-Template5.2024.docx\" target=\"_blank\">Email</a><em>, </em><a href=\"https://research.tcu.edu/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/TCU-Flier-Template.docx\" target=\"_blank\">flyer</a><em>, and </em><em><a href=\"https://research.tcu.edu/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/TCU-Recruitment-Template.docx\" target=\"_blank\">advertisement templates</a> are available on our</em><a href=\"https://research.tcu.edu/research-compliance/irb/irb-forms-templates/\" target=\"_blank\"> website</a><em>. </em>",
            "description": "<em><strong>Please note: When creating recruitment materials, please be mindful of the margins in all documents and keep the bottom right corner clear. This will ensure that the approval stamp does not cover what participants need&nbsp;to see clearly.&nbsp;</strong></em>",
            "required": true,
            "helpText": "",
            "label": "",
            "type": "attachment",
            "dependencies": [
              {
                "targetId": 3862648,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862654,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862655,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862649,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862650,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862651,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862652,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862658,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862659,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862656,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862653,
                "type": "displayed"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862666,
            "name": "TextBox1",
            "text": "<em>Please list who will serve as the point of contact who will distribute your recruitment material.</em>",
            "description": "<em><strong>NOTE: </strong>For research in which non-study team members distribute recruitment messages on behalf of the study team (e.g., distribution on a listserve, \"snowball\" sampling, etc.), it is recommended that those individuals pass along a message that includes study team member contact information. In this way, interested individuals (potential subjects) can initiate contact without having their private information exchanged without their specific consent.</em><br>",
            "required": false,
            "helpText": "",
            "label": "",
            "type": "textbox",
            "dependencies": [
              {
                "targetId": 3862656,
                "type": "displayed"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "dataId": 3862667,
                "name": "AttachButton1",
                "text": "<em>Attach the recruitment email asking your point of contact to distribute your recruitment.</em>",
                "description": "",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "attachment"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862668,
            "name": "AttachButton5",
            "text": "Please attached the&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://research.tcu.edu/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/Sona-Advertisement-Form-Approved-by-IRB-board-4.3.2020-2.docx\" target=\"_blank\">SONA advertisement form.</a><br>",
            "description": "",
            "required": false,
            "helpText": "",
            "label": "",
            "type": "attachment",
            "dependencies": [
              {
                "targetId": 3862654,
                "type": "displayed"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862669,
            "name": "TextArea11",
            "text": "<ol><li>Will investigators prospectively collect information to recruit potential participants for this study prior to consent? If so, please explain this process,&nbsp;<strong>then;&nbsp;</strong></li><li>Describe what identifiable information the study will collect for&nbsp;recruitment purposes. <em>(For example, will they collect email addresses to send out recruitment messages/materials)</em></li><li>&nbsp;What will happen with data collected for recruitment purposes? Explain reasons for keeping the data or describe how it will be destroyed.&nbsp;</li></ol>",
            "required": false,
            "helpText": "",
            "label": "",
            "type": "textarea",
            "dependencies": [
              {
                "targetId": 3862658,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862659,
                "type": "displayed"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862670,
            "name": "Group33",
            "text": "<strong>Screening</strong>",
            "description": "<em>If screening involves collecting private information about subjects, consent must be obtained prior to screening and the consent form should advise subjects that they may be withdrawn if they do not meet eligibility criteria.<br><br>Will study investigators collect information about subjects prior to enrollment in order to determine eligibility/exclude ineligible subjects? Select all that apply.</em>",
            "required": true,
            "helpText": "",
            "compoundType": "checkbox",
            "label": "",
            "type": "question",
            "dependencies": [
              {
                "targetId": 3862657,
                "type": "displayed"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "dataId": 3862671,
                "name": "CheckBox3",
                "text": "Subjects will be informed of eligibility criteria via recruitment materials and will \"self-screen\" as part of recruitment procedures. For example, using the<br><a href=\"https://cse.tcu.edu/psychology/undergraduate/sona-systems.php\" target=\"_blank\">TCU Psychology Department Research Pool</a> (SONA Systems).",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox"
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862672,
                "name": "CheckBox4",
                "text": "Yes, participants will undergo screening to determine study eligibility.<br><br>",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862673,
                    "name": "TextArea10",
                    "text": "<ol><li>Provide a complete description of study screening procedures( e.g., telephone interview, online questionnaire, etc.). </li><li>This should include how, when, where, and by whom potential participants will be screened.</li><li>Specify if you will collect identifiable, non-identifiable information, or both&nbsp;for screening purposes.</li><li>How long will the screening process take</li></ol>",
                    "required": true,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "textarea",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862672,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862674,
                    "name": "TextArea12",
                    "text": "<ol><li>Explain what you will do with the data for people who turn out to not be eligible for your study or are eligible and decide not to participate.</li><li> Describe if the data collected for screening&nbsp;will be retained separate from study data, combined with study data, or destroyed.</li></ol>",
                    "required": true,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "textarea",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862672,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862675,
                    "name": "AttachButton40",
                    "text": "<strong>Upload Screening Consent Script &Screneing Data collection sheet or document</strong>",
                    "description": "<em>The screening Consent Script templates (Treatment and Non-Treatment)&nbsp; are available on our&nbsp;<a href=\"https://research.tcu.edu/research-compliance/irb/irb-forms-templates/\" target=\"_blank\">website</a>. For more information, see Help text (?).&nbsp;</em>",
                    "required": true,
                    "helpText": "<strong>Screening consent</strong> is a crucial component of human subject research, ensuring ethical and legal compliance. It serves several important purposes:<br><br><strong>Protecting Participant Rights</strong><br><ul><li><strong>Informed Decision-Making:</strong> Even though screening doesn't involve the core research procedures, participants should understand the nature of the screening process, potential risks, and benefits. This empowers them to make an informed decision about whether to participate.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Respect for Autonomy</strong>: By obtaining consent, researchers acknowledge participants' right to self-determination and control over their personal information.</li></ul><strong>Ensuring Research Integrity<br></strong><br><ul><li><strong>Minimizing Risk:</strong> Identifying potential risks early in the process allows researchers to take appropriate precautions or exclude participants who may be at increased risk.</li></ul><strong>Legal and Ethical Compliance<br></strong><br><ul><li><strong>Regulatory Adherence:</strong> Most research regulations require informed consent for any interaction with potential or enrolled participants, including screening.</li><li><strong>Ethical Principles: </strong>Screening consent aligns with ethical principles like respect for persons, beneficence, and justice, ensuring that participants are treated fairly and ethically.</li></ul>In essence, screening consent is a fundamental step in safeguarding participant rights, maintaining research integrity, and upholding ethical and legal standards in human subject research.<br><br>",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "attachment",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862672,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
