                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862795,
                "name": "CheckBox56",
                "text": "Audio and/or video&nbsp;recordings",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862796,
                    "name": "Group69",
                    "text": "Indicate how and where the recordings will occur.",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "compoundType": "checkbox",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "question",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862795,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ],
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "dataId": 3862797,
                        "name": "CheckBox57",
                        "text": "In-person with audio/- or video-recording equipment",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "checkbox",
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "dataId": 3862798,
                            "name": "TextArea40",
                            "text": "<ol><li>Describe the recording procedures.&nbsp;</li><li>If transcribing data please indicate and provide the name of the person(s) or service/vendor that will conduct the transcription. Noting what data will be sent to the transcription service.</li></ol>",
                            "required": false,
                            "helpText": "",
                            "label": "",
                            "type": "textarea",
                            "dependencies": [
                              {
                                "targetId": 3862797,
                                "type": "displayed"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "dataId": 3862799,
                        "name": "CheckBox64",
                        "text": "Remotely using a TCU Zoom Account",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "checkbox",
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "dataId": 3862800,
                            "name": "Group70",
                            "text": "<br>Provide affirmation that study investigators will only access Zoom using their TCU login credentials.",
                            "required": false,
                            "helpText": "",
                            "compoundType": "checkbox",
                            "label": "",
                            "type": "question",
                            "dependencies": [
                              {
                                "targetId": 3862799,
                                "type": "displayed"
                              }
                            ],
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "dataId": 3862801,
                                "name": "CheckBox71",
                                "text": "<em><em>Study investigators will only access Zoom using their TCU login credentials</em>.<br></em>",
                                "required": false,
                                "helpText": "",
                                "label": "",
                                "type": "checkbox"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862802,
                    "name": "TextArea41",
                    "text": "<div><br><br></div><ol><li>Describe data security measures that will be implemented to ensure the protection of the recordings as they occur, and if any necessary transfers.</li><li>Describe how and where the recordings will be stored including data security measures that will be implemented to ensure protection.</li><li>Describe how and when the recordings will be destroyed.</li></ol>",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "textarea",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862795,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862803,
                "name": "CheckBox58",
                "text": "Ethnographic Observations",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862804,
                    "name": "TextArea43",
                    "text": "Explain how and where you will take notes on naturally occurring interaction and conversations among [place/people/situation] and if you will participate.<br>",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "<ul><li>Participant observation may require a<a href=\"https://research.tcu.edu/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/Letter-of-Support-Guidelines_8.2021.docx\" target=\"_blank\"> Letter of Support&nbsp;</a>from a ?gatekeeper? of the institution/organization involved (e.g. the director, owner, manager). </li><li>Participant observation and observation usually require informed consent from participants as well.  If it is not feasible to present each individual with a written consent form, think about how you might make people aware of your research and give them the opportunity to opt out of participation (such as by using a Study Information Sheet).  If they opt out, do not include them in your notes or project.</li><li>Observation in a public place does not require informed consent as long as:<ul><li>Those observed are not children</li><li>The observations are recorded in a manner such that the subjects cannot be identified</li><li>The observations could not reasonably place the subject at risk (legal, financial, employment, reputation) if they became known outside the research.</li></ul></li></ul>",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "textarea",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862803,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862805,
                "name": "CheckBox59",
                "text": "Physiological measure (EEG, Dexa)",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862806,
                    "name": "TextArea42",
                    "text": "<ol><li>Please describe the procedure that will be used and the part of the body that will be scanned.&nbsp;</li><li>Please explain and justify the data that will be collected and the number of scans needed to answer the research questions.&nbsp;</li></ol>",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "textarea",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862805,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862807,
                "name": "CheckBox60",
                "text": "Biospecimens (blood & saliva)",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862808,
                    "name": "Label17",
                    "text": "The TCU IRB follows&nbsp;NIH Guidelines requiring IBC review for any genetic engineering research that receives NIH funding or takes place at sites receiving NIH funding. Regardless of funding if you will be working with Recombinant DNA and synthetic nucleic acid molecules, Infectious agents, Biological toxins, or <strong>Human-derived tissues, fluids (blood or saliva), cells;&nbsp;</strong>an IBC application must be submitted and approved prior to receipt of IRB approval.<br><br>",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "label",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862807,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862809,
                    "name": "Group47",
                    "text": "Have you already received IBC approval for the work you will perform as a part of this study?",
                    "description": "<strong>Please note</strong>: <em>If samples are being collected at an off-campus facility or external institution, TCU IBC approval is not required. However, all other applicable questions in this section must be addressed.&nbsp;</em>",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "compoundType": "radio",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "question",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862807,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ],
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "dataId": 3862810,
                        "name": "Radio43",
                        "text": "Yes",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "radio",
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "dataId": 3862811,
                            "name": "TextArea49",
                            "text": "<strong>Collection & Handling</strong>",
                            "description": "<em><em>Describe the information to be gathered and the means for collecting and recording data/specimens. Be sure to address:</em><br><ul><li><em>Where and how will data or specimens be stored?</em></li><li><em>What information will be included in that data or associated with the specimens?</em></li><li><em>How long will the data or specimens be stored?</em></li><li><em>Who is responsible for the receipt or transmission of the data or specimens?</em></li><li><em>How will data and specimens be transported?</em></li><li><em>If previously collected data is to be used, describe both the previous and proposed uses of these data.</em></li></ul></em>",
                            "required": false,
                            "helpText": "",
                            "label": "",
                            "type": "textarea",
                            "dependencies": [
                              {
                                "targetId": 3862810,
                                "type": "displayed"
                              }
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "dataId": 3862812,
                            "name": "TextBox5",
                            "text": "Please provide the IBC study number.",
                            "required": false,
                            "helpText": "",
                            "label": "",
                            "type": "textbox",
                            "dependencies": [
                              {
                                "targetId": 3862810,
                                "type": "displayed"
                              }
                            ],
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "dataId": 3862813,
                                "name": "AttachButton4",
                                "text": "Please upload your IBC Approval letter.",
                                "required": false,
                                "helpText": "",
                                "label": "",
                                "type": "attachment"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "dataId": 3862814,
                        "name": "Radio44",
                        "text": "No",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "radio",
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "dataId": 3862815,
                            "name": "Label18",
                            "text": "<strong>Please review the Biosafety website for guidelines and policies, submission process and deadlines, training, and IBC forms and Templates.&nbsp; Please note IRB approval will be held until IBC approval has been obtained.&nbsp;<br><br>For questions about the IBC please email the IBC Chair, Mike Bernas at IBC@tcu.edu.</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;",
                            "required": false,
                            "helpText": "",
                            "label": "",
                            "type": "label",
                            "dependencies": [
                              {
                                "targetId": 3862814,
                                "type": "displayed"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862816,
                    "name": "Group35",
                    "text": "Will the collected biological specimens undergo genetic testing?",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "compoundType": "radio",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "question",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862807,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ],
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "dataId": 3862817,
                        "name": "Radio29",
                        "text": "Yes",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "radio",
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "dataId": 3862818,
                            "name": "TextArea33",
                            "text": "<ol><li>Provide the testing location and indicate whether or not the testing labs used is&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.fda.gov/medical-devices/ivd-regulatory-assistance/clinical-laboratory-improvement-amendments-clia\" target=\"_blank\">CLIA certified</a>.</li><li>Please indicate if genetic test results will be returned to participants or their physicians?</li><li>Provide detail regarding specifically what results will be returned, to whom they will be returned, and how they will be returned.</li><li>Please indicate if this study is part of a Genome-Wide Association Study (GWAS) and whether the data will be forwarded to the NIH dbGaP.</li></ol>",
                            "required": false,
                            "helpText": "",
                            "label": "",
                            "type": "textarea",
                            "dependencies": [
                              {
                                "targetId": 3862817,
                                "type": "displayed"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "dataId": 3862819,
                        "name": "Radio30",
                        "text": "No",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "radio"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862820,
                    "name": "TextArea32",
                    "text": "Please address each question if collecting and/or analyzing biological specimens, describe:<br><br><ol><li>How will the biological specimens be or have been collected?</li><li>How the biological specimens will be stored and where?</li><li>How long the biological specimens will be stored?</li><li>How long the biological specimens will be used?</li><li>Provide the testing location and indicate whether or not the testing labs used is <a href=\"https://www.fda.gov/medical-devices/ivd-regulatory-assistance/clinical-laboratory-improvement-amendments-clia\" target=\"_blank\">CLIA certified</a> or if testing will be done on campus provide the lab location on-campus.</li></ol>If you plan to ship biological samples to a relying institution, you need to provide a Material Transfer Agreement for each site. (Please contact the Office of Sponsored Programs at <a href=\"mailto:%22SponsoredPrograms@tcu.edu%22\" target=\"_blank\">sponsoredprograms@tcu.edu</a> to request an MTA)&nbsp;<br><br><em style=\"background-color: initial;\"><strong>Please note that MTAs can be submitted via an amendment. Be sure to state that the fully executed MTA will be submitted via an amendment before any samples are shipped.</strong></em><br>",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "textarea",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862807,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ],
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "dataId": 3862821,
                        "name": "AttachButton10",
                        "text": "Attach fully executed MTA.",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "attachment"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862822,
                "name": "CheckBox118",
                "text": "Devices (Non-medical)",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox"
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862823,
                "name": "CheckBox121",
                "text": "Randomization",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862824,
                    "name": "TextArea77",
                    "text": "Describe how randomization will be carried out in this study.",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "textarea",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862823,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862825,
                "name": "CheckBox122",
                "text": "Blinding",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862826,
                    "name": "TextArea78",
                    "text": "Describe study blinding, including whether the trial is single-blind or double-blind.",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "textarea",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862825,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862827,
                "name": "CheckBox63",
                "text": "Placebo or control group",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862828,
                    "name": "TextArea48",
                    "text": "Describe the use of a placebo or control group (e.g., lack of behavioral intervention) and provide a rationale for its use.",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "textarea",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862827,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862829,
                "name": "CheckBox1",
                "text": "Clinical Trial & FDA Regulated Studies",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862830,
                    "name": "Group84",
                    "text": "<strong>Definitions/information relevant to completing this section can be found by clicking the checkbox next to each item in the list below.&nbsp;<br></strong><br>",
                    "description": "CT.gov: Mandatory registration applies to studies meeting the definition of an \"<a href=\"https://research.tcu.edu/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/ClincalTrials.gov-Guidance-Document.docx\" target=\"_blank\">Applicable Clinical Trial</a>\"<br><br>Correctly identifying whether study activities are FDA-regulated and/or whether they meet the National Institutes of Health (NIH) definition of clinical trial ensures compliance with appropriate policies and regulations.<br><br>The US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) regulates clinical investigations conducted on test articles (drugs, biologics, devices, diagnostics, and, in some cases, dietary supplements and food additives). All such research studies must be conducted per FDA requirements for protecting human subjects and IRBs, regardless of funding source.<br><br>However, when FDA-regulated test articles are used in research conducted at TCU funded by another agency, more than one set of regulations may apply. For example, NIH-funded clinical trials fall under the jurisdiction of the FDA and the DHHS Office for Human Research Protections (OHRP). Such research must comply with the FDA and the DHHS human subject regulations.<br><br><strong>Please use the activity below to help determine if the regulations are appropriate if needed.</strong><br>",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "compoundType": "checkbox",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "question",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862829,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ],
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "dataId": 3862831,
                        "name": "CheckBox14",
                        "text": "FDA regulated clinical Investigation",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "checkbox",
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "dataId": 3862832,
                            "name": "Group119",
                            "text": "The FDA defines clinical investigation (research) as any experiment that involves a test article and one or more human subjects that either must meet the requirements for prior submission to the FDA or the results of which are intended to be later submitted to, or held for inspection by, the FDA as part of an application for a research or marketing permit.<br><br>",
                            "required": false,
                            "helpText": "",
                            "compoundType": "checkbox",
                            "label": "",
                            "type": "question",
                            "dependencies": [
                              {
                                "targetId": 3862831,
                                "type": "displayed"
                              }
                            ],
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "dataId": 3862833,
                                "name": "CheckBox130",
                                "text": "I need to know if study activities are FDA-regulated.&nbsp;",
                                "required": false,
                                "helpText": "",
                                "label": "",
                                "type": "checkbox"
                              }
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "dataId": 3862834,
                            "name": "Group120",
                            "text": "<br>First, determine whether the study activities involve an FDA-regulated test article by indicating which of the following are true. Select all that apply.<br>",
                            "required": false,
                            "helpText": "",
                            "compoundType": "checkbox",
                            "label": "",
                            "type": "question",
                            "dependencies": [
                              {
                                "targetId": 3862833,
                                "type": "displayed"
                              }
                            ],
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "dataId": 3862835,
                                "name": "CheckBox235",
                                "text": "The activity involves the use of a <a href=\"https://www.fda.gov/regulatory-information/search-fda-guidance-documents/classification-products-drugs-and-devices-and-additional-product-classification-issues#drug\" target=\"_blank\">drug</a> other than the use of a marketed drug in the course of medical practice.<br><br><br>",
                                "required": false,
                                "helpText": "",
                                "label": "",
                                "type": "checkbox"
                              },
                              {
                                "dataId": 3862836,
                                "name": "CheckBox236",
                                "text": "The activity involves the use of a <a href=\"https://www.fda.gov/regulatory-information/search-fda-guidance-documents/classification-products-drugs-and-devices-and-additional-product-classification-issues#device\" target=\"_blank\">device</a> to evaluate the safety or effectiveness of the device.<br><br><br>",
                                "required": false,
                                "helpText": "",
                                "label": "",
                                "type": "checkbox"
                              },
                              {
                                "dataId": 3862837,
                                "name": "CheckBox237",
                                "text": "Data from the activity will be submitted to, or held for inspection by, the FDA in support of a marketing or research application for an FDA-regulated product.<br><br><br>",
                                "required": false,
                                "helpText": "",
                                "label": "",
                                "type": "checkbox"
                              },
                              {
                                "dataId": 3862838,
                                "name": "CheckBox238",
                                "text": "The data obtained from control subjects will be submitted to or held for inspection by the FDA to support a marketing or research application for an FDA-regulated product.<br><br><br>",
                                "required": false,
                                "helpText": "",
                                "label": "",
                                "type": "checkbox"
                              },
                              {
                                "dataId": 3862839,
                                "name": "CheckBox239",
                                "text": "The data obtained from the use of a device on tissue specimens will be submitted to, or held for inspection by, the FDA in support of a marketing application or research application for an FDA-regulated product.<br><br><br>",
                                "required": false,
                                "helpText": "",
                                "label": "",
                                "type": "checkbox"
                              },
                              {
                                "dataId": 3862840,
                                "name": "CheckBox240",
                                "text": "None of the above",
                                "required": false,
                                "helpText": "",
                                "label": "",
                                "type": "checkbox"
                              }
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "dataId": 3862841,
                            "name": "Label30",
                            "text": "<strong>Study activities appear to be FDA-regulated. Be sure to select FDA-regulated when responding to the questions below.<br></strong>",
                            "required": false,
                            "helpText": "",
                            "label": "",
                            "type": "label",
                            "dependencies": [
                              {
                                "targetId": 3862839,
                                "type": "displayed"
                              },
                              {
                                "targetId": 3862838,
                                "type": "displayed"
                              },
                              {
                                "targetId": 3862837,
                                "type": "displayed"
                              },
                              {
                                "targetId": 3862836,
                                "type": "displayed"
                              },
                              {
                                "targetId": 3862835,
                                "type": "displayed"
                              }
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "dataId": 3862842,
                            "name": "Label29",
                            "text": "<strong>Study activities do not appear to be FDA-regulated. <strong>Select \"Study activities <strong>are not</strong> FDA regulated.\" below.</strong><br></strong>",
                            "required": false,
                            "helpText": "",
                            "label": "",
                            "type": "label",
                            "dependencies": [
                              {
                                "targetId": 3862840,
                                "type": "displayed"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "dataId": 3862843,
                        "name": "CheckBox127",
                        "text": "NIH-funded Clinical Trial",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "checkbox",
                        "dependencies": [
                          {
                            "targetId": 3862829,
                            "type": "displayed"
                          }
                        ],
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "dataId": 3862844,
                            "name": "Group121",
                            "text": "<br>The <a href=\"https://grants.nih.gov/policy/clinical-trials/definition.htm\" target=\"_blank\">NIH defines a clinical trial</a> as a research study in which one or more human subjects are prospectively assigned to one or more interventions (which may include placebo or other control) to evaluate the effects of those interventions on health-related biomedical or behavioral outcomes. If the study is not designed to assess whether a prospectively assigned intervention modifies a behavioral outcome, the study is not a clinical trial.<br><br><br><br>",
                            "required": false,
                            "helpText": "",
                            "compoundType": "checkbox",
                            "label": "",
                            "type": "question",
                            "dependencies": [
                              {
                                "targetId": 3862843,
                                "type": "displayed"
                              }
                            ],
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "dataId": 3862845,
                                "name": "CheckBox241",
                                "text": "I need to know if the NIH definition of a clinical trial is applicable to the study activities.<br>",
                                "required": false,
                                "helpText": "",
                                "label": "",
                                "type": "checkbox"
                              }
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "dataId": 3862846,
                            "name": "Label31",
                            "text": "Activities meet the definition of an NIH clinical trial when <strong>all</strong> of the following are <strong>TRUE</strong>:<br><br><ul><li>The study is supported by an <a href=\"https://www.nih.gov/institutes-nih/list-nih-institutes-centers-offices\" target=\"_blank\">NIH Institute, Center or Office</a>.</li><li>The study activities involve human participants.</li><li>The participants are prospectively assigned to an intervention.</li><li>The study activities are designed to evaluate the effect of the intervention on the participants.</li><li>The effect being evaluated is a health-related biomedical or behavioral outcome.</li></ul><br>Study activities meet the NIH definition of a clinical trial, even if:<br><br><ul><li>Healthy participants are studied.</li><li>The study does not have a comparison group (e.g., placebo or control).</li><li>The study is only designed to assess the pharmacokinetics, safety, and/or maximum tolerated dose of an investigational drug.</li><li>The study is utilizing a behavioral intervention.</li><li>Only one aim or sub-aim of your study meets the clinical trial definition.</li></ul><br><strong>NOTE</strong>:<br><ul><li>Studies intended solely to refine measures are not considered clinical trials.</li><li>Studies that involve secondary research with biological specimens or health information are not clinical trials.</li></ul>",
                            "required": false,
                            "helpText": "",
                            "label": "",
                            "type": "label",
                            "dependencies": [
                              {
                                "targetId": 3862845,
                                "type": "displayed"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862847,
                "name": "CheckBox132",
                "text": "Follow-up",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox"
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862848,
                "name": "CheckBox124",
                "text": "Other",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "checkbox",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862849,
                    "name": "TextArea79",
                    "text": "Please describe",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "textarea",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862848,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862850,
            "name": "Group94",
            "text": "<strong>Clinical Trial</strong>",
            "description": "In order to help ORC determine which federal regulations are appropriate for the review of the proposed study, indicate which of the following is true.<br><br><strong>NOTE: </strong>If you are unsure you can review the definitions above.<br>",
            "required": false,
            "helpText": "",
            "compoundType": "radio",
            "label": "",
            "type": "question",
            "dependencies": [
              {
                "targetId": 3862829,
                "type": "displayed"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "dataId": 3862851,
                "name": "Radio118",
                "text": "Study activities <strong>are</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>FDA -Regulated",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "radio",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862852,
                    "name": "Group122",
                    "text": "Select the option(s) that best describes the study. <br><br><strong>NOTE: </strong>If you are unsure, you can review the definitions above.<br>",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "compoundType": "checkbox",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "question",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862851,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ],
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "dataId": 3862853,
                        "name": "CheckBox242",
                        "text": "FDA-regulated Clinical Investigation - A research study involving:<br><br><ul><li>Drugs</li><li>Biologics</li><li>Medical devices</li><li>Human food</li><li>Electronic product</li><br></ul>",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "checkbox"
                      },
                      {
                        "dataId": 3862854,
                        "name": "CheckBox243",
                        "text": "NIH-funded Clinical Trial - A research study, funded by the NIH, in which one or more human subjects are prospectively assigned to one or more interventions (which may include placebo or other control) to evaluate the effects of those interventions on health-related biomedical or behavioral outcomes.<br>",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "checkbox",
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "dataId": 3862855,
                            "name": "Label33",
                            "text": "<strong>Training<br>Any investigators involved in conducting an NIH-sponsored clinical trial must complete training in Good Clinical Practices. The requirement can be met at UC Santa Cruz by completing one of the following <a href=\"https://www.citiprogram.org/Shibboleth.sso/Login?target=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.citiprogram.org%2FSecure%2FWelcome.cfm?inst=952&entityID=urn:mace:incommon:ucsc.edu\" target=\"_blank\">CITI Program</a> online human subjects research optional training courses:<br><br><ul><li>GCP - Social and Behavioral Research Best Practices for Clinical Research (ID: 146855).</li><li>Good Clinical Practice Course (US FDA focus) (ID: 75054).</li><li>GCP Course for Clinical Trials Involving Investigational Drugs (international / ICH focus) (ID: 75052).</li><li>GCP Course for Clinical Trials Involving Investigational Medical Devices (international focus) (ID: 75053).</li></ul><strong>NOTE: All study investigators must complete the appropriate course</strong> before the study can be approved/exempt certified.</strong>",
                            "required": false,
                            "helpText": "",
                            "label": "",
                            "type": "label",
                            "dependencies": [
                              {
                                "targetId": 3862854,
                                "type": "displayed"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862856,
                "name": "Radio119",
                "text": "Study Activities <strong>are not</strong> FDA-regulated",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "radio",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862857,
                    "name": "Group124",
                    "text": "",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "compoundType": "radio",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "question",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862856,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ],
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "dataId": 3862858,
                        "name": "Radio74",
                        "text": "Study activities <strong>meet</strong> the NIH definition of a clinical trial.",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "radio",
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "dataId": 3862859,
                            "name": "Label32",
                            "text": "<strong>Training<br>Any investigators involved in conducting an NIH-sponsored clinical trial must complete training in Good Clinical Practices. The requirement can be met at UC Santa Cruz by completing one of the following <a href=\"https://www.citiprogram.org/Shibboleth.sso/Login?target=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.citiprogram.org%2FSecure%2FWelcome.cfm?inst=952&entityID=urn:mace:incommon:ucsc.edu\" target=\"_blank\">CITI Program</a> online human subjects research optional training courses:<br><br><ul><li>GCP - Social and Behavioral Research Best Practices for Clinical Research (ID: 146855).</li><li>Good Clinical Practice Course (US FDA focus) (ID: 75054).</li><li>GCP Course for Clinical Trials Involving Investigational Drugs (international / ICH focus) (ID: 75052).</li><li>GCP Course for Clinical Trials Involving Investigational Medical Devices (international focus) (ID: 75053).</li></ul><strong>NOTE: All study investigators must complete the appropriate course</strong>&nbsp;before the study can be approved/exempt certified.</strong>",
                            "required": false,
                            "helpText": "",
                            "label": "",
                            "type": "label",
                            "dependencies": [
                              {
                                "targetId": 3862858,
                                "type": "displayed"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "dataId": 3862860,
                        "name": "Radio75",
                        "text": "Study activities<strong> do not meet</strong> the NIH definition of a clinical trial.",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "radio"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862861,
            "name": "Group75",
            "text": "<strong>Sharing Results with Participants</strong>",
            "description": "<em>Will study results or individual subject results be shared with subjects or their providers (e.g., incidental findings, results of standard or research lab tests, genetic test results, etc.)?</em>",
            "required": false,
            "helpText": "",
            "compoundType": "radio",
            "label": "",
            "type": "question",
            "dependencies": [
              {
                "targetId": 3862851,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862829,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862807,
                "type": "displayed"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "dataId": 3862862,
                "name": "Radio4",
                "text": "Yes",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "radio"
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862863,
                "name": "Radio5",
                "text": "No",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "radio"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862864,
            "name": "TextArea47",
            "text": "<strong>Procedures for Sharing Results</strong>",
            "description": "<em>Describe what results may be shared and how. If the study carries a risk of incidental findings, describe your plan for evaluating these and determining whether and how subjects or their providers will be given this information.</em>",
            "required": false,
            "helpText": "",
            "label": "",
            "type": "textarea",
            "dependencies": [
              {
                "targetId": 3862862,
                "type": "displayed"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862865,
            "name": "Group76",
            "text": "<strong>CLIA Certified Laboratory Results</strong>",
            "description": "<em>If laboratory results will be shared with subjects or their healthcare providers, confirm if the laboratory conducting the test is CLIA certified.</em>",
            "required": false,
            "helpText": "",
            "compoundType": "radio",
            "label": "",
            "type": "question",
            "dependencies": [
              {
                "targetId": 3862862,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862829,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862807,
                "type": "displayed"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "dataId": 3862866,
                "name": "Radio65",
                "text": "Yes",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "radio"
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862867,
                "name": "Radio66",
                "text": "No",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "radio"
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862868,
                "name": "Radio70",
                "text": "N/A",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "radio"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862869,
            "name": "TextArea17",
            "text": "<strong>Study Procedures</strong>",
            "description": "Provide a chronological (step-by-step)&nbsp;description/outline in lay terms of the procedures, tests, and interventions that will be implemented during the study, from the initial screening to the final follow-up visit.<br><br><b style=\"font-style: italic;\">Be sure to include, as applicable to the study:</b><br><ul><li><em>When are all research procedures being performed? Including the timing and amount of all samples collected for research purposes.</em></li><li><em>Describe the duration of study participation, the length and number of study visits, and the timetable for study completion.<br></em></li><li><em style=\"background-color: initial;\">Please clarify the sequence and timing of each procedure, including their estimated duration and frequency.<br></em></li><li><em style=\"background-color: initial;\">Which procedures will be conducted for research as opposed to standard-of-care procedures? In determining what procedures are research vs. standard of care, consider what procedures would happen to any participant who joins the study versus procedures that would occur exactly as described in the protocol, even if the individual does not join the study.</em></li><li><em style=\"background-color: initial;\">Specify what types of data will be collected and how they will be collected (e.g., surveys, interviews, physical measurements), including long-term follow-up.</em></li><li><em>Describe if there will be any stopping criteria due to any potential safety concerns for participants or members of the study team</em></li><li><em>All drugs and devices used in the research and the purpose of their use.</em></li><li><em>Include information on dosage and administration methods<br></em></li><li><em>If applicable, please provide a detailed description of any interventions or treatments administered during the study.</em></li><li><em>Please detail the follow-up procedures, including the frequency and duration of follow-up visits or contacts<br></em></li><li><em>Explain how participant adherence to the study protocol will be monitored and encouraged. (schedule of events?)<br></em></li><li><em>Procedures that will be followed when subjects withdraw from the research, including withdrawal from intervention but continued data collection.</em></li><li><em>Any anticipated circumstances under which subjects will be withdrawn from the research without their consent.</em></li></ul>",
            "required": true,
            "helpText": "",
            "label": "",
            "type": "textarea",
            "dependencies": [
              {
                "targetId": 3862762,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
                "targetId": 3862765,
                "type": "displayed"
              },
              {
