                        "text": "Analyzing study data",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "checkbox"
                      },
                      {
                        "dataId": 3862977,
                        "name": "CheckBox115",
                        "text": "Other",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "checkbox"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862978,
                    "name": "TextArea39",
                    "text": "Please describe what will be done differently at each site.&nbsp;e.g., not enrolling minors, not collecting specimens, different recruitment methods.<br>",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "textarea",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862977,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862979,
                    "name": "AttachButton20",
                    "text": "Alternatively, you may include an attachment listing the sites and what will be done differently at each site.<br>",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "attachment",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862969,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862980,
            "name": "Group37",
            "text": "Will any investigators from the relying institution be involved in the use of human blood, body fluids, tissues, or cells (including cell lines) by drawing samples, accepting samples already drawn, receiving samples from any source, or in any other way?",
            "required": true,
            "helpText": "",
            "compoundType": "radio",
            "label": "",
            "type": "question",
            "children": [
              {
                "dataId": 3862981,
                "name": "Radio87",
                "text": "Yes",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "radio",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862982,
                    "name": "TextArea57",
                    "text": "Provide information&nbsp; regarding :<br><br><ol><li>Will biological samples be collected at the relying institution or shipped to the relying institution? Identify the lab and lab location.</li><li>If you plan to ship biological samples to a relying institution, have you need to provide a Material Transfer Agreement for each site. (Please contact the Office of Sponsored Programs at&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:%22SponsoredPrograms@tcu.edu%22\" target=\"_blank\">sponsoredprograms@tcu.edu</a> to request an MTA) <em><strong>Please note MTAs can be submitted via an amendment. Be sure to state that the fully executed MTA will be submitted via an amendment before any samples are shipped.</strong></em></li><li>Be specific about what kind of biological samples will be shipped and what test will be conducted at each site.&nbsp;</li></ol>",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "textarea",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862981,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ],
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "dataId": 3862983,
                        "name": "AttachButton21",
                        "text": "Attach fully executed MTA.",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "attachment"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862984,
                "name": "Radio88",
                "text": "No",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "radio"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862985,
            "name": "Group72",
            "text": "Were any conflicts of interest (COIs) disclosed by investigators at the relying institution(s)?<br>",
            "required": true,
            "helpText": "",
            "compoundType": "radio",
            "label": "",
            "type": "question",
            "children": [
              {
                "dataId": 3862986,
                "name": "Radio92",
                "text": "Yes - One or more COIs were disclosed",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "radio"
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862987,
                "name": "Radio93",
                "text": "No",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "radio"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862988,
            "name": "Group82",
            "text": "How did the relying institution handle the COI disclosure(s)?<br>",
            "required": true,
            "helpText": "",
            "compoundType": "radio",
            "label": "",
            "type": "question",
            "dependencies": [
              {
                "targetId": 3862986,
                "type": "displayed"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "dataId": 3862989,
                "name": "Radio94",
                "text": "The relying institution <strong>did not require </strong>any management measures affecting research design, such as requiring the interest to be disclosed in consent forms.<br>",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "radio"
              },
              {
                "dataId": 3862990,
                "name": "Radio95",
                "text": "The relying institution <strong>required</strong> management measures affecting research design, such as requiring the interest to be disclosed in consent forms.<br>",
                "required": false,
                "helpText": "",
                "label": "",
                "type": "radio",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "dataId": 3862991,
                    "name": "TextArea58",
                    "text": "Provide details of the COI management measures or attach a description of the COI management plan. <br><strong>NOTE:</strong><br><ul><li>Do NOT provide details of the interest beyond management measures.</li><li>If providing via an attachment enter \"N/A\".</li></ul>",
                    "required": false,
                    "helpText": "",
                    "label": "",
                    "type": "textarea",
                    "dependencies": [
                      {
                        "targetId": 3862990,
                        "type": "displayed"
                      }
                    ],
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "dataId": 3862992,
                        "name": "AttachButton22",
                        "text": "Attach COI Management plans, if applicable.",
                        "required": false,
                        "helpText": "",
                        "label": "",
                        "type": "attachment"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862993,
            "name": "TextArea56",
            "text": "Please provide&nbsp;Participating sites' IRB/HRPP contact name, title, and email address",
            "required": true,
            "helpText": "",
            "label": "",
            "type": "textarea",
            "dependencies": [
              {
                "targetId": 3862407,
                "type": "displayed"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "dataId": 3862994,
        "name": "Section16",
        "text": "Multi-Site (Relying)",
        "label": "",
        "type": "question",
        "dependencies": [
          {
            "targetId": 3862408,
            "type": "displayed"
          }
        ],
        "children": [
          {
            "dataId": 3862995,
            "name": "Label2",
            "text": "You have indicated that one or more external institutions and/or external investigators will be engaged in human subjects research for this study.<br><br>Research may involve more than one institution and be within the responsibility of more than one Institutional Review Board (IRB). If this study involves research with a collaborating external institution(s) or investigator(s), check  the help text first to see  if TCU and the collaborating external institution(s)/investigator(s) are considered to be engaged in research. Institutions/investigators not engaged in research do not need IRB review for their research.",
            "required": false,
            "helpText": "In general, an institution is considered engaged in a particular non-exempt human subjects research project when its employees or agents for the purposes of the research project obtain: <br>(1) data about the subjects of the research through intervention or interaction with them; <br>(2) identifiable private information about the subjects of the research; or <br>(3) the informed consent of human subjects for the research.<br>More specifically, an institution is engaged in research when ANY of the following apply:<br><br><ul><li>The institution is the awardee institution for a non-exempt human subjects research project, even if all activities will be carried out by employees or agents of another institution.</li><li>An employee or agent of the institution intervenes with human subjects for research purposes through</li><li>Invasive or noninvasive procedures (see examples below)</li><li>Manipulating the environment  (see examples below)</li><li>Interacting with any human subject of the research (see examples below)</li><li>Obtaining informed consent</li><li>Obtaining identifiable private information or identifiable specimens, even if there is no direct interaction with human subjects (see examples below)</li></ul><br>Examples of <em>invasive or noninvasive procedures</em> include:<br><ul><li>drawing blood;</li><li>collecting buccal mucosa cells using a cotton swab;</li><li>administering individual or group counseling or psychotherapy;</li><li>administering drugs or other treatments;</li><li>surgically implanting medical devices;</li><li>utilizing physical sensors;</li><li>utilizing other measurement procedures.</li></ul>Examples of <em>manipulating the environment </em>include:<br><ul><li>controlling environmental light, sound, or temperature;</li><li>presenting sensory stimuli;</li><li>orchestrating environmental events or social interactions.</li></ul>Examples of <em>interacting</em> include:<br><ul><li>engaging in protocol dictated communication or interpersonal contact;</li><li>asking someone to provide a specimen by voiding or spitting into a specimen container;</li><li>conducting research interviews or administering questionnaires.</li></ul>Obtaining <em>identifiable private information</em> or <em>identifiable specimens</em> includes, but is not limited to:<br><ul><li>observing or recording private behavior;</li><li>using, studying, or analyzing for research purposes identifiable private information or identifiable specimens provided by another institution; and</li><li>using, studying, or analyzing for research purposes identifiable private information or identifiable specimens already in the possession of the investigators&nbsp;</li></ul>",
            "label": "",
            "type": "label"
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862996,
            "name": "Group86",
            "text": "<strong>Collaborating Investigator(s) at External Institution(s)</strong>",
            "description": "If multiple institutions are engaged in the research, each institution's IRB may review the research independently, or you may request that only one IRB reviews the research for multiple institutions in what is called a Reliance Agreement or IRB Authorization Agreement (IAA). TCU may agree to one of the following arrangements:<br><br><ul><li>The TCU IRB <strong>relies</strong> on the other institution's IRB review of the research, or</li><li>The TCU IRB <strong>reviews</strong> the research for the other institution's IRB.</li></ul>In order to establish a reliance agreement, all institutions involved must agree to the reliance and each institution's internal requirements must also be met. The institution whose IRB reviews the research serves as the \"IRB of Record.\"<br><br>The TCU IRB will <strong>rely on </strong>another institution's IRB;<strong> another institution's IRB will serve as the IRB of Record.</strong><br><br><strong>Note: </strong><br><ul><li>The TCU IRB only relies on institutions that hold a <a href=\"https://www.hhs.gov/ohrp/register-irbs-and-obtain-fwas/fwas/fwa-protection-of-human-subjecct/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">Federal-wide Assurance(FWA)</a></li></ul>If you wish to have the TCU IRB consider entering into a reliance agreement for this study:<br><br><ol><li>Review the <a href=\"https://research.tcu.edu/research-compliance/irb/reliance/\" target=\"_blank\">Office of Research Compliance Reliance page</a> for information on our reliance procedures.</li><li>Reach out to the external institution <strong>early in the application process</strong> to see if their IRB would be open to a reliance agreement with TCU.</li><li>Some institutions will not enter into a reliance agreement if the study qualifies for exemption from IRB review, you should reach out to the external institution early in the application process to find this out.</li><li>Determine what method of documenting the reliance is preferred. Typically this is done by contacting the external institution's study Principal Investigator or human subjects protections/IRB office.</li></ol>",
            "required": false,
            "helpText": "",
            "label": "",
            "type": "question"
          },
          {
            "dataId": 3862997,
            "name": "Group87",
            "text": "<strong>Method of Initiating Reliance</strong>",
            "description": "In most cases, reliance agreements with non-TCU institutions are documented via the SMART IRB online reliance system. In some cases, an Institutional Authorization Agreement (IAA) may be utilized. The IAA must be signed by the institutional officials (IOs) at both institutions. <br><br>The Reviewing IRB will usually dictate how they would like the agreement documented. You should reach out to the external institution early in the application process to see if their IRB would be open to a reliance agreement with TCU, and to determine what method of documenting the reliance is preferred. Typically, this can be determined by contacting the external institution's study Principal Investigator or human subjects protections/IRB office.<br><br><strong>Please select the type of agreement requested.</strong>",
            "required": true,
            "helpText": "",
            "compoundType": "radio",
            "label": "",
            "type": "question",
            "children": [
              {
